# 📚 Stacks & Queues (Part 1) - Introduction to Stack

## 📌 Introduction

A **Stack** is a linear data structure that follows the **LIFO (Last In, First Out)** principle.

This means the **last element inserted is the first one to be removed.**

Think of a stack of books:

- You place a new book on the top.
- You remove the top book first.

Stacks are one of the most frequently used data structures in programming and interviews.

