# 💡 Interview Tips

✅ Stack follows the **LIFO** principle.

✅ All operations occur only at the **Top**.

✅ Push inserts an element.

✅ Pop removes the top element.

✅ Peek returns the top element without removing it.

---

# ⚠️ Common Mistakes

❌ Popping from an empty stack.

❌ Pushing into a full array-based stack.

❌ Forgetting to update the Top pointer.

❌ Confusing Stack (LIFO) with Queue (FIFO).

---

# 📝 Summary

- A Stack is a linear data structure based on the LIFO principle.
- Insertion and deletion happen only at the Top.
- Push, Pop, and Peek all work in **O(1)** time.
- Stacks are widely used in recursion, browser history, expression evaluation, and DFS.
- They can be implemented using arrays or linked lists.

